  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Isolated planets <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> have masses <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M_{X}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M_{Y}\"></span> respectively and are separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>. A point P is located at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{3}\"></span> from planet <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>, as shown. The gravitational field strength at P is zero.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M_{Y}}{M_{X}}\"></span>?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">2</li><li data-label=\"B\">3</li><li data-label=\"C\">4</li><li data-label=\"D\">9</li></ol>"
